+# Verification checklist: create-and-scene
+
+This merges lead IDs `L-1` through `L-68` and implementor IDs `I-1` through `I-49`. Shared behaviors retain both IDs; an original ID appears in multiple rows when it covered several behaviors. `C-*` rows cover definition requirements neither checklist explicitly checked. Source records provenance, not verification status. Evidence files are in the run output `evidence/` directory.
+
+References are relative to this change: ESP = `specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md`, PS = `specs/presentation-skill/spec.md`, PV = `specs/presentation-verification/spec.md`. Project workflow references use the repository's `AGENTS.md` (called `CLAUDE.md` in the inputs). Unit and component tests run under fast `npm test`; only the test plan's INT-001/INT-002 and E2E-001/E2E-002 run under separate `test:integration` and `test:e2e` scripts. `npm run verify` is the production browser gate. Skill-procedure checks inspect the normative instructions in `SKILL.md` and structurally test each obligation; mere keyword presence is insufficient. These checks do not have an agent execute the skill or judge browser screenshots. Screenshot files and advisory diagnostics are tested as artifacts, not proof of visual quality.
+
+The lead resolved the differing readings within the approved definition and recorded them in `/workspace/home/.agent-runner/projects/-artifacts--runtime-candidate-worktree/runs/audited-implement-change-2026-10-23T15-18-38-746838863Z/output/acceptance-assumptions.md`. Applied rulings: DOM-node persistence is required within the same group and Scene; other transitions use shared-layout projection. Scale is step-independent at a fixed viewport/mode and recomputes on resize. Unknown routes show Landing; trailing slashes are tolerated. Any scaffolding into a non-empty project requires a stated target and confirmation; fully scaffolded projects skip scaffolding. No user decision is pending.
